o end it' challenged as needing 'no safe way', since DESIGN-NOTES says terminate() IS reachable. NOT changed, and the comment now says why: terminate() does not END the extraction, it parks the promise for ever and stops the shared queue draining for the life of the process, so there is no affordance that ends this document safe or otherwise, and 'no safe way' would invite the question whose answer is 'and then nothing indexes until you restart Zotero'. (d) The SDT_BLOCKED_PHASES.includes mutant was hand-run and not committed, so the claim resting on it was not re-derivable by make sitter-mutants; it is now M49f in the probe. Manifest 0.4.25 -> 0.4.26: the guard reddened on the comment-only edits above, exactly as this ticket's Action 8 says it would.
